<https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation/connection-edge-node>
    inv:alternativeRule "Directed indication, adornments, end labels, elaboration and proxy connections remain unillustrated." ;
    inv:attachmentRule "The binary grammar uses connection-end, which can be a usage-node or usage-edge." ;
    inv:compartmentRule "The full connection node can contain a compartment stack, omitted in the minimal redraw." ;
    inv:condition "The redraw covers a connection usage node and undirected binary representation; it is not the definition-edge or binding notation." ;
    inv:coverageClaim inv:RepresentativeOnly ;
    inv:geometry "Rounded full connection usage node or binary line joining connection ends." ;
    inv:illustratedForms "Undirected binary connection line and minimal full connection usage node." ;
    inv:labelRule "The node uses connection-name-compartment; the edge has an optional connection-label. Role names, multiplicities and c-adornment are separate grammar elements." ;
    inv:lineStyle "Solid line for the binary example; optional direction-indication arrow is not drawn and does not by itself assert flow semantics." ;
    inv:representedKinds "SysML ConnectionUsage" ;
    inv:supportingProduction <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/connection-end/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/connection-graphical/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/connection-label/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/connection-name-compartment/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/connection/1> ;
    inv:supportingSourceCell <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation-source/table-11/cell-5>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation-source/table-11/cell-6> .

<https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation/connection-nary>
    inv:alternativeRule "The definition dot/segments are separate productions. End labels and all cardinality/context rules need a full audit." ;
    inv:attachmentRule "Each n-ary-segment links the central n-ary-connection-dot to a usage-node." ;
    inv:compartmentRule "This record describes the n-ary relationship form rather than a full node compartment stack." ;
    inv:condition "Representative n-ary usage connection; do not substitute the separate n-ary definition grammar or infer arbitrary endpoint semantics." ;
    inv:coverageClaim inv:RepresentativeOnly ;
    inv:geometry "Filled central dot with segments to usage nodes, as described in the graphical grammar." ;
    inv:illustratedForms "No local redraw" ;
    inv:labelRule "Central cdot-label uses UsageDeclaration; each segment has role name and multiplicity elements." ;
    inv:lineStyle "Solid segments; source description only, without a local redraw." ;
    inv:representedKinds "SysML ConnectionUsage with multiple ends" ;
    inv:supportingProduction <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/cdot-label/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/n-ary-connection-dot/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/n-ary-connection/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.13/n-ary-segment/1> ;
    inv:supportingSourceCell <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation-source/table-11/cell-8> .

<https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation/part-definition-node>
    inv:alternativeRule "Boundary ports, additional prefixes, aliases and compartment contents remain to be audited separately." ;
    inv:attachmentRule "The part-def production provides top, bottom, left and right port positions; these remain unillustrated." ;
    inv:compartmentRule "Interconnection contents and a compartment stack may extend the definition node; omitted in the minimal redraw." ;
    inv:condition "Represents a part definition rather than a particular usage of that definition." ;
    inv:coverageClaim inv:RepresentativeOnly ;
    inv:geometry "Sharp-corner rectangular definition node." ;
    inv:illustratedForms "Minimal part definition node with keyword and name." ;
    inv:labelRule "Definition prefix, part def keyword and definition-name-with-alias; the minimal example uses «part def»." ;
    inv:lineStyle "Solid outline in the original redraw." ;
    inv:representedKinds "SysML PartDefinition" ;
    inv:supportingProduction <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.11/part-def-name-compartment/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.11/part-def/1> ;
    inv:supportingSourceCell <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation-source/table-9/cell-1> .

<https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation/part-node>
    inv:alternativeRule "Composite and referential forms are grouped here. Compartment contents, boundary attachments and prefix combinations need further audit." ;
    inv:attachmentRule "port-t, port-b, port-l and port-r positions are permitted by the part production; side ports are not illustrated here." ;
    inv:compartmentRule "The grammar permits an interconnection view and compartment stack. These are not fully illustrated." ;
    inv:condition "A referential part remains a PartUsage. The redraw demonstrates outline and label forms, not every permitted part context." ;
    inv:coverageClaim inv:RepresentativeOnly ;
    inv:geometry "Rounded rectangular usage node; the illustrated composite and reference forms share the same basic geometry." ;
    inv:illustratedForms "One solid composite part node and one dashed referential part node." ;
    inv:labelRule "Part usage prefix and name/type follow part-name-compartment and usage-name-with-alias; the example uses «part» and «ref part»." ;
    inv:lineStyle "Solid outline for the composite example; dashed outline for the reference example." ;
    inv:representedKinds "SysML PartUsage" ;
    inv:supportingProduction <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.11/part-name-compartment/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.11/part-ref/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/graphical-production/8.2.3.11/part/1> ;
    inv:supportingSourceCell <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation-source/table-9/cell-2> .

<https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation/port-node-boundary>
    inv:alternativeRule "All four orientations, direction glyphs, nesting and proxy alternatives require distinct checks. No direction is inferred from the undirected glyph." ;
    inv:attachmentRule "The grammar gives separate left, right, top and bottom boundary productions with position-specific labels." ;
    inv:compartmentRule "Full nodes can have a compartment stack and nested ports. Neither is exhausted by the illustration." ;
    inv:condition "Use boundary position and optional direction indications according to the corresponding port production; one drawn position does not cover all four." ;
    inv:coverageClaim inv:RepresentativeOnly ;
    inv:geometry "Full rounded usage node or small rounded boundary glyph. The boundary redraw illustrates one attachment position." ;
    inv:illustratedForms "Full port usage node and a single compact boundary-port example." ;
    inv:labelRule "The full form uses the port-name-compartment. Boundary labels use QualifiedName with an optional colon and QualifiedName." ;
    inv:lineStyle "Solid node and boundary glyph in the redraw; directional arrows are omitted." ;
    inv:representedKinds "SysML PortUsage" ;
